GROUNDS OF APPEAL:
4. The impugned judgment has been challenged on the ground that the same is bad in law and fact since it fails to take into account order dated 22.11.2017 passed by the Hon'ble High Court of Delhi in Cr. Misc. Case No. 3018 of 2017 between the same parties wherein the Hon'ble High Court is pleased to observe that "it is also noted that litigation regarding loan transaction are pending between the petitioner and respondent"; that the impugned judgment ignored the police report dated 16.05.2017 in CC no. 39 u/s. 406/420 IPC filed by the complainant against the appellant wherein police reported that complainant gave Rs.25,00,000/- only to the appellant on 17.05.2013;
that Ld. Trial Court fell into error while observing that the stand of the accused is that complainant failed to prove the document dated 17.05.2013 whereas said document was never acted upon; that complainant himself deposed that he was not aware of the contents of the said document as he does not CA No. 77/2019 BIRENDRA SHUKLA VS. VIRENDRA RANA PAGE NO. 3 OF 25 understand English
